

⭐ Overlay Panel — Full Specification

This panel controls every visual layer that sits on top of the cinematic viewport.Each layer is a toggleable, configurable module with its own rendering logic.

🔶 1. Panel Structure

The panel is organized into five collapsible groups, each representing a category of overlays:

Time Fields

Meta‑Model Regimes

Organisms

Metric & Geometry

Blueprint HUD

Each group contains multiple layers with:

toggle

opacity slider

color map selector

detail level

blending mode

⭐ 2. Time Fields Group

This group visualizes the core time fabric.

Layers:

Θ Field Heatmap

Shows dilation/compression

Color maps: plasma, inferno, viridis

Options: smoothing, thresholding

Θ Gradient Vectors

Shows direction of time‑flow distortion

Options: vector density, arrow size

Time Curvature Map

Derived from ∂²Θ

Highlights warp boundaries and frozen pockets

These layers reveal the texture of time.

⭐ 3. Meta‑Model Regimes Group

This group visualizes the Ξ field, which determines which time model is active.

Layers:

Ξ Regime Map

Colors regions by active time model

Example:

Classical = blue

Relativistic = red

Warp = purple

Frozen = cyan

Regime Boundaries

Draws outlines where Ξ changes

Useful for meta‑equation debugging

Regime Stability Map

Shows stable / metastable / unstable zones

This group makes the meta‑equation visible.

⭐ 4. Organisms Group

This group visualizes field organisms — warp bubbles, time crystals, frozen pockets, etc.

Layers:

Organism Outlines

Draws boundaries of each organism

Organism Heatmap

Shows organism influence strength

Organism Labels

Shows name, ID, lifecycle stage

Organism Trails

Shows movement paths over time

This group reveals the living structures inside the time fabric.

⭐ 5. Metric & Geometry Group

This group visualizes the metric field and geometric distortions.

Layers:

Metric Grid

Warped grid lines

Options: density, thickness

Curvature Map

Shows Ricci or scalar curvature

Lightcone Overlay

Shows local causal structure

This group reveals the geometric skeleton of the simulation.

⭐ 6. Blueprint HUD Group

This group overlays blueprint metadata directly on the viewport.

Layers:

Active Blueprint Snippet

Shows the DSL code that generated the current frame

Time Model Info

Shows the active TimeModel interface values

Meta‑Equation State

Shows G(Ξ, Θ, g, ρ) values

Observer HUD

Shows Δτ, velocity, local Θ, local Ξ

This group turns the viewer into a simulation debugger.

⭐ 7. Layer Controls (Universal)

Every layer has:

Toggle (on/off)

Opacity slider (0–100%)

Color map selector

Detail level (low/med/high)

Blending mode

Add

Multiply

Screen

Overlay

Difference

These controls give you cinematic + scientific flexibility.

⭐ 8. Interaction Model

The Overlay Panel supports:

Shift‑click → solo a layer

Alt‑click → isolate a group

Drag to reorder layers

Right‑click → layer settings

This gives you fast, intuitive control during analysis.



